#!/usr/bin/env python3
# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""octl — agent-facing opencode CLI (opencode-ctl).

One process per invocation. JSON goes to stdout, human logs go to stderr and the
process exit code classifies the outcome (see ``EXIT_*``). It drives an
operator-deployed ``opencode serve`` over HTTP using the shared, stdlib-only
``octl_core`` domain library.

Security invariants (DESIGN-opencode-ctl.zh-CN.md §2):

* no credential material is ever written to stdout, stderr or a log line, under
  any code path (success, error or debug);
* endpoints are addressed by alias only — there is no URL parameter anywhere;
* there is no session-listing verb and no endpoint registration verb.

Requires Python >= 3.11 (``tomllib``), standard library only.
"""

